// Fictional, static training curriculum. No executable evidence.
// Imported functions only: application state remains in main.ks.
module curriculum

func curriculumJSON() { emit "{\"cases\":[{\"id\":\"account\",\"number\":\"01\",\"title\":\"An identity out of place\",\"category\":\"Account compromise\",\"icon\":\"fingerprint\",\"level\":\"Foundational\",\"duration\":\"25–35 min\",\"color\":\"purple\",\"org\":\"Aster Healthworks\",\"role\":\"Identity & access analyst\",\"summary\":\"A finance account. An unfamiliar sign-in. A quiet inbox rule. Follow the trail before the next payment run.\",\"brief\":\"The service desk escalated a sign-in alert for Maya Chen, a finance coordinator at Aster Healthworks. Payroll closes at 12:00 UTC. Determine whether the account was misused, contain access, and give finance a defensible assessment of payment risk.\",\"objectives\":[\"Correlate identity and mailbox records\",\"Separate account misuse from proven data loss\",\"Contain sessions while preserving evidence\"],\"context\":\"All timestamps: 14 May 2026, UTC. Maya normally works from a managed device on 192.0.2.24. The supplied logs are a partial collection, not a complete audit. Geographic labels are simulator metadata; IP location alone cannot identify an attacker.\",\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"A1\",\"type\":\"Login log\",\"title\":\"An unfamiliar successful sign-in\",\"time\":\"08:42\",\"source\":\"Identity provider · authentication log\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"The identity provider recorded a successful sign-in to Maya’s account from an unmanaged device.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The record directly supports the successful sign-in and unmanaged status. It does not prove who operated the device or where they were physically located.\",\"body\":\"event_id: AUTH-2187\\nuser: maya.chen@aster.example\\ntime: 2026-05-14T08:42:00Z\\nresult: SUCCESS\\nip: 203.0.113.42\\ndevice: unmanaged / browser\\nregion_label: unfamiliar\\nauthentication: password + push approval\\nsession_id: S-8841\"},{\"id\":\"A2\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"“I did not sign in”\",\"time\":\"09:04\",\"source\":\"Service desk · employee statement\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"Maya’s message proves that a specific external person controlled her account.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"Maya denies the activity and reports approving a push, but this statement cannot establish the operator’s identity. Validate the report through a trusted contact channel.\",\"body\":\"From: maya.chen@aster.example\\nTo: helpdesk@aster.example\\nDate: 2026-05-14 09:04 UTC\\nSubject: Repeated sign-in prompts\\n\\nI got several phone prompts around 08:40 and approved one to make them stop. I did not sign in this morning. I am traveling and my work laptop is off. Can someone call my registered number?\"},{\"id\":\"A3\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"External forwarding rule created\",\"time\":\"08:47\",\"source\":\"Mail platform · audit event\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"A forwarding rule was created in the same session as the unfamiliar sign-in.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The matching session_id links these events. Rule creation is confirmed; actual message delivery requires message-trace evidence.\",\"body\":\"event: New-InboxRule\\ntime: 2026-05-14T08:47:00Z\\nactor: maya.chen@aster.example\\nsession_id: S-8841\\nrule_name: Archive receipts\\nmatch: subject contains invoice OR payment\\naction: forward to receipts@ledger-sync.example\\nmove_to: Archive\\nstatus: enabled\"},{\"id\":\"A4\",\"type\":\"Login log\",\"title\":\"Known device baseline\",\"time\":\"08:15\",\"source\":\"Identity provider · prior-day baseline\",\"severity\":\"Info\",\"claim\":\"The new sign-in differs from Maya’s supplied baseline.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The baseline shows a managed device and a different address. A baseline difference is an indicator, not sufficient proof of compromise by itself.\",\"date\":\"2026-05-13\",\"body\":\"time: 2026-05-13T08:15:00Z\\nuser: maya.chen@aster.example\\nresult: SUCCESS\\nip: 192.0.2.24\\ndevice: AST-LT-044 / managed\\nauthentication: password + push approval\\nnetwork: corporate office\"},{\"id\":\"A5\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"Mailbox access observed\",\"time\":\"08:50\",\"source\":\"Mail platform · access audit\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"An operator may have sought payment information.\",\"expected\":\"inference\",\"why\":\"Access to payment-related messages and the rule’s keywords support this hypothesis. Intent and downstream use are not directly observed.\",\"body\":\"event: MailItemsAccessed\\ntime: 2026-05-14T08:50:00Z\\nsession_id: S-8841\\nfolder: Finance/Payments\\nitems_accessed: 12\\nsubject_examples: May vendor payments; Payroll approval\\nmessage_trace: NOT INCLUDED\\nattachment_download_telemetry: NOT INCLUDED\"},{\"id\":\"A6\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"Finance needs an answer\",\"time\":\"09:12\",\"source\":\"Finance operations · internal message\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"A fraudulent payment has already been completed.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"Finance reports a pending payment run and no confirmed loss. Access creates exposure; it does not establish that a payment changed or funds were lost.\",\"body\":\"From: finance.lead@aster.example\\nTo: incident.desk@aster.example\\nDate: 2026-05-14 09:12 UTC\\nSubject: Payroll and vendor payment exposure\\n\\nThe next payment run is scheduled for 12:00 UTC. Maya can prepare payment files but cannot approve release alone. We have not confirmed any changed bank details or lost funds. Please advise whether we should pause approvals.\"}],\"decisions\":[{\"id\":\"contain\",\"title\":\"Contain the account\",\"prompt\":\"What is your first coordinated response?\",\"hint\":\"A password reset may leave existing sessions active. Think about identity, session access, and evidence.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Reset the password and close the incident.\",\"explanation\":\"A reset alone does not address every active session or the forwarding rule. Preserve audit records, revoke sessions, and investigate mailbox changes before closure.\"},{\"label\":\"Preserve logs, restrict sign-in, revoke sessions, and coordinate a credential reset and MFA review.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"This limits further access while retaining records for scope analysis. Validate Maya through a trusted channel; document the forwarding rule before removing it. Restriction can disrupt finance work, so provide an approved alternate workflow.\"},{\"label\":\"Delete the mailbox to prevent further access.\",\"explanation\":\"Deleting the mailbox destroys useful evidence and disrupts operations. Target access and the unauthorized rule; retain mailbox records under the organization’s process.\"}]},{\"id\":\"scope\",\"title\":\"State the scope honestly\",\"prompt\":\"Which finding belongs in your update to finance?\",\"hint\":\"A recorded mailbox read and a rule do not prove successful forwarding or payment fraud.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"All payroll data was stolen and funds are lost.\",\"explanation\":\"Neither complete data theft nor a financial transfer is established. This overstatement can trigger disproportionate decisions and undermine trust.\"},{\"label\":\"No risk exists because payments need two approvers.\",\"explanation\":\"Dual approval is a mitigating control, not proof of safety. Exposed payment context could support fraud attempts or sensitive-data access.\"},{\"label\":\"Suspicious access and a forwarding rule are confirmed; delivered messages and financial loss remain unverified.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"A1, A3, and A5 establish activity. Obtain message traces, mailbox-change history, and payment approval records to bound exposure. Ask finance to independently verify changed bank details and temporarily hold suspect approvals.\"}]},{\"id\":\"recover\",\"title\":\"Return the account to service\",\"prompt\":\"What evidence supports safe recovery?\",\"hint\":\"Recovery needs validation of the affected controls and continued monitoring, not simply a quiet alert queue.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Verify sessions revoked, rule removed, credentials and MFA secured; monitor and coordinate finance review.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"Record containment results and timestamps, verify with Maya through a trusted channel, review other mailbox changes, and monitor fresh activity. Finance should reconcile payment changes and authorize resumption; absence of new alerts alone is not proof of eradication.\"},{\"label\":\"Wait one hour without alerts, then restore everything.\",\"explanation\":\"A quiet hour does not validate session revocation, rule removal, or credential security. Recovery must check that the entry route and persistence were addressed.\"},{\"label\":\"Block only 203.0.113.42 permanently.\",\"explanation\":\"An address block may supplement controls, but the operator could change networks. Identity and mailbox controls address the observed access more directly.\"}]}],\"debrief\":\"The defensible assessment is likely account compromise: Maya’s denial, the unfamiliar session, mailbox reads, and the forwarding rule reinforce one another. The operator’s identity, delivered forwarding, and payment loss remain unknown. Contain access, preserve traces, and involve finance before payment release.\",\"business\":\"Payment diversion exposure, sensitive finance information, and payroll disruption; actual financial loss remains unconfirmed.\",\"next\":\"Request mail delivery traces and payment-change records. Validate with Maya by registered contact. Review other sessions, OAuth grants, and mailbox rules.\",\"exemplar\":\"A1 records a successful unmanaged sign-in at 08:42 UTC. A3 links a forwarding rule to session S-8841, and A5 records access to 12 finance messages. Account misuse is likely given Maya’s denial (A2); operator identity and successful forwarding remain unverified. Revoke sessions, restrict sign-in, preserve audit records, and remove the documented rule. Finance should verify bank-detail changes before the 12:00 payment run (A6). Request message traces and reconcile payment approvals before declaring loss or closing the incident.\"},{\"id\":\"phishing\",\"number\":\"02\",\"title\":\"The invoice that didn’t belong\",\"category\":\"Phishing investigation\",\"icon\":\"mail\",\"level\":\"Intermediate\",\"duration\":\"25–35 min\",\"color\":\"green\",\"org\":\"Juniper Design Co.\",\"role\":\"Email security analyst\",\"summary\":\"A familiar supplier name hides an unfamiliar destination. Work out who clicked, what ran, and what remains unknown.\",\"brief\":\"An employee reported an invoice email at Juniper Design Co. One colleague clicked its link before the warning circulated. Analyze the message, correlate the user activity, and scope a proportionate response without assuming a click means a compromised account.\",\"objectives\":[\"Inspect sender and link inconsistencies\",\"Correlate mail, proxy, and identity evidence\",\"Scope a campaign without assuming credential theft\"],\"context\":\"All timestamps: 18 June 2026, UTC. The real supplier in this simulation uses northstar.example. A click log shows navigation, not what a person typed. Do not visit sample URLs; they are inert training text.\",\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"P1\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"A supplier’s urgent invoice\",\"time\":\"10:02\",\"source\":\"Reported message · raw headers and body\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"The displayed supplier identity and actual sender domain differ.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The display name names Northstar, while the sending address and reply-to use other domains. Authentication passes for the sending domain, not for the claimed supplier.\",\"body\":\"From: \\\"Northstar Billing\\\" <billing@northstar-docs.example>\\nReply-To: collections@accounts-review.example\\nTo: purchasing@juniper.example\\nDate: 2026-06-18 10:02 UTC\\nSubject: ACTION REQUIRED: Invoice 4021 overdue\\nAuthentication-Results: spf=pass; dkim=pass; dmarc=pass (northstar-docs.example)\\n\\nYour service will stop today. Review invoice 4021 and sign in with your work account.\\nDisplayed link: https://northstar.example/invoice/4021\\nActual href: https://secure-invoice.example/review/4021\"},{\"id\":\"P2\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"Message delivery scope\",\"time\":\"10:03\",\"source\":\"Mail gateway · campaign query\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"The supplied gateway query identified eight delivered copies of this message.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The query result supports eight deliveries for the queried message fingerprint. It does not rule out related messages with different fingerprints.\",\"body\":\"query_time: 2026-06-18T10:03:00Z\\nmessage_fingerprint: SIM-MSG-4021\\ndelivered: 8\\nquarantined: 0\\nrecipient_group: Purchasing\\nattachment_count: 0\\nrelated_campaign_query: NOT RUN\"},{\"id\":\"P3\",\"type\":\"Login log\",\"title\":\"One observed link visit\",\"time\":\"10:07\",\"source\":\"Web proxy · navigation event\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"Leo submitted his password to the destination.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"A GET request confirms a visit. It cannot establish form submission or credential entry. Obtain a trusted user statement and relevant identity telemetry.\",\"body\":\"time: 2026-06-18T10:07:00Z\\nuser: leo.park@juniper.example\\ndevice: JUN-LT-18\\nmethod: GET\\nurl: https://secure-invoice.example/review/4021\\nresponse: 200\\ncontent_label: work-account sign-in page\\nPOST_body_capture: disabled\\ndownload_events: none observed in supplied interval\"},{\"id\":\"P4\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"The recipient’s account\",\"time\":\"10:11\",\"source\":\"Service desk · employee report\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"Credential harvesting is a plausible purpose of the message.\",\"expected\":\"inference\",\"why\":\"The impersonation, destination mismatch, and sign-in page support this hypothesis. The sender’s actual intent is inferred; credential theft is not confirmed.\",\"body\":\"From: leo.park@juniper.example\\nTo: helpdesk@juniper.example\\nDate: 2026-06-18 10:11 UTC\\nSubject: Invoice link looked strange\\n\\nI opened the invoice. It asked for my work password, which seemed odd. I think I closed the tab before entering anything, but I was in a rush. Please check. I have not received any MFA prompts.\"},{\"id\":\"P5\",\"type\":\"Login log\",\"title\":\"Identity review window\",\"time\":\"10:20\",\"source\":\"Identity provider · scoped search\",\"severity\":\"Info\",\"claim\":\"Leo’s account can be declared safe for all future activity.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"The query covers a short interval. No unfamiliar sign-in in that interval reduces immediate concern but does not establish no disclosure or future misuse.\",\"body\":\"query_at: 2026-06-18T10:20:00Z\\nwindow: 10:00–10:20 UTC\\nuser: leo.park@juniper.example\\nknown_device_signins: 1\\nunfamiliar_signins: 0\\nnew_MFA_enrollments: 0\\nnew_OAuth_grants: 0\\ncoverage_after_10:20: NOT AVAILABLE\"},{\"id\":\"P6\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"Supplier confirms a mismatch\",\"time\":\"10:25\",\"source\":\"Purchasing · trusted-channel verification\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"Purchasing reports the supplier disavowed invoice 4021 through an established contact.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"This records a trusted-channel verification, strengthening the impersonation finding. It does not reveal the sender’s identity or prove credentials were collected.\",\"body\":\"From: purchasing.lead@juniper.example\\nTo: incident.desk@juniper.example\\nDate: 2026-06-18 10:25 UTC\\nSubject: Supplier verification\\n\\nI called Northstar using the number in our vendor register, not the email. They did not send invoice 4021 and do not use northstar-docs.example. Our actual renewal is next month. Please avoid blocking all supplier correspondence; two legitimate orders are due today.\"}],\"decisions\":[{\"id\":\"contain\",\"title\":\"Stop further exposure\",\"prompt\":\"How should you contain this campaign?\",\"hint\":\"Use the message fingerprint and destination indicators. Preserve the original before removal.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Preserve the email, quarantine matching copies, block the malicious destination, and warn recipients.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"P1 and P6 support a targeted response. Preserve headers and delivery records; search for variants beyond the exact fingerprint. Notify purchasing through trusted channels. Broad supplier blocking could delay legitimate orders.\"},{\"label\":\"Allow it because SPF, DKIM, and DMARC passed.\",\"explanation\":\"Authentication passed for northstar-docs.example, the sending domain. That does not verify the claimed supplier or make the content trustworthy.\"},{\"label\":\"Block all external email for the entire organization indefinitely.\",\"explanation\":\"This is disproportionate to the available scope and would disrupt operations. Target known indicators and expand controls if additional evidence warrants it.\"}]},{\"id\":\"scope\",\"title\":\"Investigate the clicked link\",\"prompt\":\"What is the best next step for Leo’s account?\",\"hint\":\"Separate visiting a page from submitting credentials; the user’s memory is uncertain.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Record confirmed credential theft and stop investigating.\",\"explanation\":\"P3 confirms a visit, while P4 is uncertain about entry. Calling theft confirmed overstates evidence and leaves the actual scope unresolved.\"},{\"label\":\"Contact Leo through a trusted channel, extend identity review, and apply precautionary access controls if exposure cannot be excluded.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"Clarify entry and MFA activity, inspect sessions and relevant identity events, and document the uncertainty. A credential reset and session revocation may be prudent under policy when exposure cannot be excluded; label those precautionary, not proof of theft.\"},{\"label\":\"Take no action because no unusual sign-in appeared by 10:20.\",\"explanation\":\"The short search window cannot rule out delayed misuse. Continue targeted investigation and advise Leo to report prompts or unexpected activity.\"}]},{\"id\":\"recover\",\"title\":\"Communicate and close\",\"prompt\":\"Which closure standard is defensible?\",\"hint\":\"Validate mail containment, account scope, and business continuity. Name anything still unresolved.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Close as a harmless false alarm because no attachment existed.\",\"explanation\":\"A credential-harvesting attempt can use a link without an attachment. P1, P3, and P6 support treating the message as malicious impersonation.\"},{\"label\":\"State all eight recipients lost their passwords.\",\"explanation\":\"Eight deliveries do not equal eight clicks or eight disclosures. Report the actual evidence and the coverage limits.\"},{\"label\":\"Verify quarantine and blocks, document recipient follow-up and identity review, and brief purchasing on residual uncertainty.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"Confirm actions in the relevant consoles in a real response, preserve the investigation trail, and set a monitoring owner and review window. Purchasing should use the trusted supplier channel so legitimate orders can proceed. Close only with documented disposition of Leo’s possible exposure.\"}]}],\"debrief\":\"This is a well-supported supplier-impersonation phishing attempt. Authentication of a lookalike sender does not authenticate the supplier. Eight deliveries and one observed visit are confirmed; credential disclosure and later account misuse are unresolved.\",\"business\":\"Purchasing interruption, possible credential exposure, and risk of supplier payment diversion; broad blocking could delay legitimate orders.\",\"next\":\"Follow up with Leo, extend identity review, search campaign variants, and validate quarantine. Coordinate legitimate orders through the vendor register.\",\"exemplar\":\"P1 shows a supplier display name with mismatched sender and destination domains; P6 records supplier denial via an established contact. P2 identifies eight deliveries and P3 one visit. Credential submission remains unverified because form data is unavailable and Leo is uncertain (P4). Preserve the message, quarantine matches, block the destination, and review campaign variants. Follow up on identity exposure and consider precautionary access controls. Purchasing faces order disruption and possible payment diversion; use trusted vendor contacts while monitoring continues.\"},{\"id\":\"endpoint\",\"number\":\"03\",\"title\":\"A process with a hidden agenda\",\"category\":\"Suspicious endpoint activity\",\"icon\":\"terminal\",\"level\":\"Intermediate\",\"duration\":\"30–40 min\",\"color\":\"orange\",\"org\":\"Meridian Research\",\"role\":\"Endpoint response analyst\",\"summary\":\"A script interpreter. A new scheduled task. An outbound connection. Find the chain without losing the evidence.\",\"brief\":\"An endpoint alert on a research workstation interrupted a project handoff at Meridian Research. Reconstruct the execution chain, assess persistence and possible data exposure, and recommend containment that preserves evidence and keeps the research team informed.\",\"objectives\":[\"Reconstruct a process and persistence chain\",\"Reason about network evidence and collection gaps\",\"Balance containment with research continuity\"],\"context\":\"All timestamps: 09 July 2026, UTC. Host MR-LT-27 is assigned to Sam Rivera. Research files are sensitive. This is a static simulation: no commands execute, no endpoint is connected, and no isolation is actually performed.\",\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E1\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"Document spawns a script process\",\"time\":\"14:06\",\"source\":\"Endpoint sensor · process tree\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"The sensor recorded a script interpreter launched by the document application.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The parent-child process record directly supports the chain. The chain is suspicious in this context but does not identify a malware family or actor.\",\"body\":\"time: 2026-07-09T14:06:00Z\\nhost: MR-LT-27\\nuser: sam.rivera\\nparent: WINWORD.EXE (pid 4100)\\nchild: powershell.exe (pid 4188)\\narguments: [encoded script redacted — inert simulation]\\nsource_document: Project_Brief.docm\\nsensor_action: alert only; process not blocked\"},{\"id\":\"E2\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"An unexpected project brief\",\"time\":\"14:02\",\"source\":\"Mail archive · delivered message\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"The attachment was probably the initial delivery route.\",\"expected\":\"inference\",\"why\":\"The matching filename and timing support a likely connection. A file hash correlation or direct open event would strengthen attribution to this exact message.\",\"body\":\"From: project-office@meridian-partners.example\\nTo: sam.rivera@meridian.example\\nDate: 2026-07-09 14:02 UTC\\nSubject: Updated project brief — review today\\nAttachment: Project_Brief.docm\\n\\nPlease review the attached draft before our project handoff.\\n\\nArchive note: attachment hash not collected; sender relationship not yet verified.\"},{\"id\":\"E3\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"A task survives the process\",\"time\":\"14:08\",\"source\":\"Endpoint sensor · scheduled task event\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"A scheduled task was registered to run an updater script at user logon.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"The task registration confirms a persistence configuration. It does not establish that a future logon occurred or the task later executed.\",\"body\":\"time: 2026-07-09T14:08:00Z\\nhost: MR-LT-27\\nevent: scheduled_task_registered\\ncreator_pid: 4188\\ntask_name: ResearchUpdate\\ntrigger: user logon\\naction: script interpreter runs user-profile updater.ps1\\nscript_hash: NOT COLLECTED\\nsubsequent_task_execution: NOT INCLUDED\"},{\"id\":\"E4\",\"type\":\"Security alert\",\"title\":\"Outbound traffic after execution\",\"time\":\"14:09\",\"source\":\"Network sensor · connection metadata\",\"severity\":\"High\",\"claim\":\"The connection proves that research documents were exfiltrated.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"A connection and byte counts establish traffic, not content. Encrypted payload inspection and file-access telemetry are absent; data theft remains unresolved.\",\"body\":\"time: 2026-07-09T14:09:00Z\\nhost: MR-LT-27\\nprocess_pid: 4188\\ndestination: 198.51.100.77:443\\nbytes_sent: 18432\\nbytes_received: 92720\\ntls_payload: not captured\\nfile_access_telemetry: unavailable\\nreputation: unknown\"},{\"id\":\"E5\",\"type\":\"Login log\",\"title\":\"A short identity review\",\"time\":\"14:13\",\"source\":\"Identity provider · scoped search\",\"severity\":\"Info\",\"claim\":\"The supplied identity search found no new remote sign-ins in its time window.\",\"expected\":\"confirmed\",\"why\":\"This is a bounded negative finding for 14:00–14:13. It neither establishes a clean endpoint nor rules out local credential access or later identity misuse.\",\"body\":\"query_at: 2026-07-09T14:13:00Z\\nuser: sam.rivera@meridian.example\\nwindow: 14:00–14:13 UTC\\nnew_remote_signins: 0\\ncredential_access_telemetry: NOT INCLUDED\\npost_window_activity: NOT AVAILABLE\"},{\"id\":\"E6\",\"type\":\"Email\",\"title\":\"The project’s deadline\",\"time\":\"14:16\",\"source\":\"Research lead · operations note\",\"severity\":\"Medium\",\"claim\":\"Isolating this host will destroy the only copy of the research.\",\"expected\":\"unresolved\",\"why\":\"The note confirms a dependency and says a synchronized copy is available. Isolation affects connectivity, not necessarily data retention. Validate backup integrity before promising availability.\",\"body\":\"From: research.lead@meridian.example\\nTo: incident.desk@meridian.example\\nDate: 2026-07-09 14:16 UTC\\nSubject: MR-LT-27 handoff dependency\\n\\nSam needs the analysis for a 16:00 partner handoff. A synchronized project copy is available in the team repository, though we have not validated the latest revision. Please coordinate an alternate workstation. No data loss has been confirmed.\"}],\"decisions\":[{\"id\":\"contain\",\"title\":\"Contain the workstation\",\"prompt\":\"What is the strongest immediate response?\",\"hint\":\"Stopping network access can limit spread. Powering off can lose volatile evidence.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Leave it online until the 16:00 deadline.\",\"explanation\":\"The process, task, and connection create ongoing risk. Coordinate an alternate workstation and evidence preservation rather than accepting uncontrolled access for the deadline.\"},{\"label\":\"Coordinate network isolation, preserve available volatile evidence, and document actions and business handoff.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"Prompt isolation reduces network exposure; use a trusted response channel and collect volatile evidence where feasible without delaying urgent containment. Record the sequence and avoid unnecessary power-off. Confirm availability of a clean workstation and repository copy.\"},{\"label\":\"Immediately wipe the disk and declare the incident resolved.\",\"explanation\":\"A wipe removes evidence before scope is established. Containment and preservation come first; rebuilding may be appropriate later with a validated recovery plan.\"}]},{\"id\":\"scope\",\"title\":\"Assess what the chain proves\",\"prompt\":\"Which conclusion and follow-up best fit the records?\",\"hint\":\"Persistence configuration is visible. The encrypted connection does not reveal transferred content.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Suspicious execution and persistence configuration are confirmed; collect scripts, file-access and network evidence to assess data exposure.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"E1 and E3 establish execution and a registered task. E4 establishes traffic, not exfiltrated documents. Safely collect file artifacts and hashes, task details, relevant memory and network records; hunt for the same indicators on other hosts.\"},{\"label\":\"Research theft is confirmed because outbound traffic used port 443.\",\"explanation\":\"Port 443 and byte counts do not identify content. Describe potential confidentiality impact while treating exfiltration as unverified.\"},{\"label\":\"The workstation is clean because no remote sign-in was found.\",\"explanation\":\"E5 is a short identity search; local execution and persistence can occur without new remote sign-ins.\"}]},{\"id\":\"recover\",\"title\":\"Recover with confidence\",\"prompt\":\"Which plan best supports a defensible return to work?\",\"hint\":\"Validate the device and the data. Assign a monitoring owner and scope follow-up.\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Delete the task and reconnect immediately.\",\"explanation\":\"The task may be only one persistence mechanism. Deleting it alone does not establish eradication or address potentially exposed credentials and artifacts.\"},{\"label\":\"Keep the host isolated forever with no business update.\",\"explanation\":\"Containment is temporary risk management. Research needs a recovery path, clear ownership, and a documented impact assessment.\"},{\"label\":\"Preserve artifacts, rebuild or remediate under policy, validate a clean recovery copy, assess credentials, and monitor before release.\",\"correct\":true,\"explanation\":\"Validate eradication or a trusted rebuild, verify the repository revision and alternate workstation, assess identity exposure, and set monitoring and approval criteria. Document any remaining scope gaps and communicate handoff implications to research leadership.\"}]}],\"debrief\":\"A document-launched interpreter, a linked logon task, and outbound traffic support a serious endpoint incident. Execution and configured persistence are confirmed. Initial delivery is inferred; research exfiltration, actor identity, and fleet-wide scope are unresolved.\",\"business\":\"Potential research confidentiality exposure and a 16:00 partner handoff delay; no confirmed data loss. Recovery must validate the shared project copy.\",\"next\":\"Collect script artifacts, task details, hashes and relevant volatile evidence. Hunt other hosts, assess identity exposure, and validate a clean research copy.\",\"exemplar\":\"E1 records document-launched script execution at 14:06 UTC. E3 links a logon task to the same process and E4 records an outbound TLS connection. The email attachment is a likely delivery route (E2), but no hash match is supplied. Research exfiltration is unverified because payload and file-access records are missing. Isolate the host while preserving evidence, collect artifacts, and hunt related activity. The 16:00 partner handoff is at risk (E6); validate the repository copy and use a clean workstation. Require validated remediation and monitoring before reconnecting.\"}],\"reportFields\":[{\"id\":\"summary\",\"label\":\"Executive summary\",\"placeholder\":\"What happened, how confident are you, and what does leadership need to know?\"},{\"id\":\"findings\",\"label\":\"Confirmed technical findings\",\"placeholder\":\"State directly supported observations. Cite evidence IDs, e.g. [A1].\"},{\"id\":\"uncertainty\",\"label\":\"Assumptions & open questions\",\"placeholder\":\"Separate plausible explanations from unknowns. What evidence would resolve each gap?\"},{\"id\":\"impact\",\"label\":\"Business impact\",\"placeholder\":\"Describe confidentiality, operational, and financial exposure. Distinguish potential from realized impact.\"},{\"id\":\"response\",\"label\":\"Response & recovery plan\",\"placeholder\":\"Proposed containment, evidence preservation, recovery checks, owners, and success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"followup\",\"label\":\"Follow-up & lessons\",\"placeholder\":\"What will you collect next? Who will review it, when, and how could controls improve?\"}]}" }
